# R2.6: an `at` line is integer-valued (N5); 8.5 names no line (x is set on lines 8 and 9).
x is 10
x is 20
print of [what is x at 8.0, what is x at 9.0, what is x at 8]
for ln in [8.5, 9.9]:
    try:
        print of ["answered", ln, what is x at ln]
    catch e:
        print of [ln, e.kind, e.message]
